7642720273342001-c1424264-0b7d-42ad-85ba-8fcd54ed317f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed via Gerrit change 2209 (MERGED, commit ae1bc8871273): LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on patchset 2. Deliverables: examples/mcp-clients/{copilot/mcp-config.json,codex/config.toml,claude/.mcp.json} (env-var bearer, no committed secret), examples/mcp-clients/README.md, docs/mcp-client-setup.md (+ docs index), and hermetic AC test tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py. AC oracles all green in CI (real list_tickets result over a loopback rebar-mcp HTTP instance with the resolved bearer; 401 on absent/invalid bearer; no-PAT-literal grep; skip-with-reason real-CLI acceptance for copilot/codex/claude). Patchset 1 Verified-1 was one unrelated wall-clock flake (test_rich_reemit_state) filed as perplexed-jeanlike-kakarikis (discovered_from).","timestamp":1787642720273342001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787594486142668001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b73ad17e-2ece-44bb-bb7a-a5a731f9df17","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fd4a-4e91-f179-4932"},{"link_uuid":"a4643ea9-c956-425d-b5f7-d876afe2cfc3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"9015-739e-e72c-4fe5"},{"link_uuid":"2f0c54c2-f24b-4d47-9577-6c3685f9e604","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f968-d1a9-33d3-4ced"},{"link_uuid":"18ee702b-7b5a-4b2d-97b2-139f23c4f21e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"14c4-7010-fca1-416d"}],"description":"Wire the copilot, codex, and claude client configs to connect to the rebar MCP endpoint over remote\nHTTP with a `static` bearer PAT (ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur; PATs from exuberant-blockish-avians).\nSingle concern: the three client-side config shapes + a basic read-tool smoke — the endpoint/edge is\nesok, the credentials are avians, live prod verification is jackal.\n\n## Relationship to the already-landed avians artifacts (no duplication)\navians already committed the repo-root placeholder template `mcp-clients.local.example.json` (copied\nto the gitignored `mcp-clients.local.json`) and the runbook `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`\n(step 4 \"Wire each client locally\", provisioning + rotation, box env vars\n`MCP_CLIENT_PAT_{COPILOT,CODEX,CLAUDE}`). This ticket does NOT restate that provisioning/rotation\nmodel; the new setup doc links to the runbook and template and adds only the missing piece — the\nconcrete per-client config SHAPE for copilot/codex/claude. The example configs reuse the same env\nvar names and the same gitignored local file.\n\n## Approach + rationale (static bearer for all three; sourced from client `--help`)\nAll three clients support a static `Authorization: Bearer <PAT>` header for a remote HTTP MCP server\nand none require OAuth, so one auth shape covers all three (surfaces verified against each client's\nown `--help` / official docs, cited in the setup doc):\n- **Copilot** (`copilot mcp add --transport http --header \"Authorization: Bearer $VAR\"`, per\n  `copilot mcp add --help`): `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` — a `type: http` rebar entry with the HTTPS\n  `/mcp/` URL and a `headers` map `Authorization: Bearer $MCP_CLIENT_PAT_COPILOT` (the CLI expands\n  `$VAR` from the environment, so no PAT literal is stored).\n- **Codex** (`bearer_token_env_var`, per developers.openai.com/codex Streamable-HTTP config):\n  `~/.codex/config.toml` — a `[mcp_servers.rebar]` streamable-HTTP entry with\n  `bearer_token_env_var = \"MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX\"` so the PAT comes from the environment.\n- **Claude** (`claude mcp add --transport http --header`, per code.claude.com/docs mcp): `.mcp.json`\n  (`type: http`, `headers` `Authorization: Bearer ${MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CLAUDE}`). Document the gotcha: a\n  static header takes precedence and does NOT fall back to OAuth if rejected, so a wrong/expired PAT\n  fails hard (not a silent OAuth retry).\nEach references the gitignored credential (env var / `mcp-clients.local.json`), never an inline\nsecret. Ship copy-ready example configs under `examples/mcp-clients/` plus a setup doc; the three\nclient-home files themselves are not committed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Tier: **real client config load + a basic read-tool call**, made hermetic by spinning up a\n  local `rebar-mcp` HTTP instance on loopback with a known static token — no network, no external\n  service. Oracles:\n  - Real-tool-result (client-agnostic, always runs in CI): a client-agnostic structural loader\n    parses each committed example config, validates it against that client's documented schema, and\n    resolves the bearer via the client's documented env-var substitution; the loopback `rebar-mcp`\n    then serves a real read tool (a ticket `show`/`list`) for the resolved `Authorization: Bearer`\n    header — oracle: a real tool result payload, not just \"connected\".\n  - Contrast (§6, always runs): the same loopback server returns 401 for an absent/invalid bearer,\n    confirming the header is actually on the request path (not a hang).\n  - Client-binary acceptance (skips-with-reason when the CLI is absent, so CI without the binaries\n    still passes): where installed, `copilot mcp get rebar` / `codex mcp list` / `claude mcp list`\n    load the committed example config and list the `rebar` server. Each such check is individually\n    guarded by `shutil.which`/`pytest.skip(\"<client> CLI not installed\")`.\n- [x] No secret is committed (the PAT is sourced from the avians env var / gitignored file); a test\n  asserts no PAT literal appears in any committed example config (only an env-var reference).\n\n## Testing / Verification\n- Proof command: `make test PYTEST_ARGS=tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py`.\n  The real-tool-result assertion, the 401 contrast, and the no-secret grep run unconditionally\n  (they need only the in-repo loopback `rebar-mcp`); the per-client CLI acceptance checks\n  skip-with-reason when that client binary is not installed, so the suite is green in a hermetic CI\n  runner that lacks copilot/codex/claude.\n- Full gate: `make lint && make typecheck && make test`.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nAdditive client config; rollback = remove the `examples/mcp-clients/` files + the setup doc. No\nserver-side change.\n\nDepends on: cibophobic-holohedral-esok (reachable endpoint), exuberant-blockish-avians (PATs).\nBlocks: creased-childlike-jackal (live prod verification).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/mcp-clients/copilot/mcp-config.json","reason":"Copy-ready Copilot CLI remote-HTTP rebar server entry (env-var bearer)"},{"path":"examples/mcp-clients/codex/config.toml","reason":"Copy-ready Codex [mcp_servers.rebar] streamable-HTTP entry (bearer_token_env_var)"},{"path":"examples/mcp-clients/claude/.mcp.json","reason":"Copy-ready Claude Code .mcp.json rebar server entry (env-var bearer header)"},{"path":"examples/mcp-clients/README.md","reason":"Wiring/rotation instructions for the three example client configs"},{"path":"docs/mcp-client-setup.md","reason":"Setup doc: connect copilot/codex/claude to the rebar MCP endpoint with a static bearer PAT"},{"path":"docs/README.md","reason":"Index the new client-setup doc"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py","reason":"Hermetic AC test: real read-tool call per client config + 401 contrast + no-secret grep"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","9015-739e-e72c-4fe5"],["depends_on","fd4a-4e91-f179-4932"],["parent","jira-reb-3527"],["relates_to","14c4-7010-fca1-416d"],["relates_to","f968-d1a9-33d3-4ced"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-3527","parent_status_uuid":"00cf2de9-3546-429c-99c8-5e10117855fa","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"14f5-ca81-b70d-4550","ticket_type":"task","title":"Wire copilot / codex / claude MCP client configs to the rebar MCP server","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6085a8f1-c7a8-4280-a9bb-f696b5cffdcf","a375889f-373f-4ee1-9690-bbe78d8a1b05","18fae93a-1951-48bc-8699-adb8d7f5e79c","b30ceba3-779a-4769-9ac3-b81ad096844d","f3e1c539-f874-4685-8778-3cea11a7eda4","5b57bddc-0f7e-4bdc-9901-0499b0d1c95f","2f0c54c2-f24b-4d47-9577-6c3685f9e604","18ee702b-7b5a-4b2d-97b2-139f23c4f21e","629c1e11-c6b7-4caa-92f9-74f5d02b937e","00cf2de9-3546-429c-99c8-5e10117855fa","e97edcbe-43b4-40f6-a836-7fe4eeca50af","c1424264-0b7d-42ad-85ba-8fcd54ed317f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787649968500378001,"uuid":"94c54d0d-6c21-4c33-b66a-4c78c65e7462"}